<section id="delivery-notes" class="section-grid">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
    <h2>Why this site is still Rust-backed</h2>
    <p>
      The point of the rebuild is not to turn the site into a frontend-only design exercise. Astro now owns content
      and presentation, while Axum remains responsible for the runtime concerns that actually benefit from a typed backend:
      asset delivery, APIs, observability, and interactive demos.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="notes-grid">
    <article class="surface-panel notes-card">
      <h3>Static-first pages</h3>
      <p>Astro handles route generation, content collections, and long-form page composition.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="surface-panel notes-card">
      <h3>Rust runtime</h3>
      <p>Axum serves the built site, the WASM bundle, the Game of Life API, and structured frontend logs.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="surface-panel notes-card">
      <h3>Operational shape</h3>
      <p>Docker still packages the Rust binary with generated frontend assets so the deployment path stays simple.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

